# QuantForg Design Freeze (post-RC4)

The QuantForg Design System is **LOCKED** on the **RC4 brand identity**.

**Product-owner override:** RC3 Design Freeze was explicitly superseded by an authorized RC4 visual rebrand. RC4 (logo-derived charcoal + cyan) is the permanent visual baseline.

## Forbidden

- Redesign or restyle existing UI beyond verified RC4 inheritance
- New visual patterns, tokens, or component chrome unrelated to RC4
- New navigation models or interaction models
- Subjective polish / “make it nicer” changes
- Pure black (`#000`) product backgrounds; neon / hacker / gaming / crypto aesthetics

## Allowed only

- Verified bugs
- Accessibility issues
- Responsive issues
- Performance regressions
- Proven usability issues discovered during testing
- Inheritance of RC4 tokens / brand mark / charcoal–cyan surfaces on new UI

## Brand baseline (RC4)

- Official mark: `frontend/public/brand/quantforg-mark.png` (+ SVG)
- Primary: turquoise / cyan (`--accent` ≈ `#00D4E0`)
- Secondary: white / silver text
- Neutrals: premium charcoal (`#111827`, `#151B23`, `#1A2330`, `#202938`)
- Ambient: subtle radial gradients — no noisy grids

## Inheritance

Every future UI must inherit from the Design Bible + **RC4** shell language (`docs/design/`, ADR-0022, shared desk chrome, IBM Plex, RC4 tokens).

Do not modify `components/terminal|book|research|counsel/` unless fixing a verified bug/a11y/responsive/perf issue above (or applying shared RC4 token inheritance only).

Tag target for the frozen frontend baseline: `v1.0.0-frontend` (visual layer: RC4).
